## 268. Missing Number

## Approach
--  Array contains numbers from 0 to n.
--  Calculate the expected sum of 0 → n using:
--  n * (n + 1) / 2
--  Calculate the actual sum of all elements in the array.
--  The difference between expected and actual sum is the missing number.
--  Return sum - s.

## Complexity 
Time: O(n) — one loop through the array.
Space: O(1) — only a couple of variables, no extra array.

SOLUTION  :
class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int sum = n * (n + 1) / 2;
        int s = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            s += nums[i];
        }
        return (sum - s);
    }
}
